# Standalone guided walk through bob/capture — a SearchTextRequest whose
# type was inferred, whose score is not perfect, and whose first text_query
# is shadowed by a second.
#
# Invocation:
#   protolens --descriptor-set alice/app.desc \
#       --script grpconf2026/beats/capture.script bob/capture
#
# Positional paths:
#   /    SearchTextRequest root (inferred, score −8)
#   /1   text_query: "<binary blob>"  — the shadowed first instance
#   /2   text_query: "coffee in Grenoble"  #@ repeated_singular
#   /3   language_code: "en-US"
#
# Re-pin (must print nothing):
#   protolens --descriptor-set alice/app.desc \
#       --script grpconf2026/beats/capture.script bob/capture script \
#     | grep 'error:'

title: What is bob/capture?

steps:
  - text: |
      protolens opened without a type name and found one anyway:

        👉 SearchTextRequest.
      
      What you see is prototext format:
      i.e., textproto format enriched with structured annotations

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /
    select_line: true
    search: SearchTextRequest

  - text: |
      Hover over the "SearchTextRequest" type name.

      A score breakdown tooltip appears.
      Note the penalty for "non-canonical encoding".

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /
    select_line: true
    search: SearchTextRequest

  - text: |
      The text_query field is the issue.
      The schema declares it singular (press `v` to verify)
      but it appears twice at wire-level.

      The first instance gets shadowed by the second:
      most tools (including protoc) will silently drop it.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /2
    select_line: true
    search: text_query

  - text: |
      protolens signals the repeated instance with
      - an amber diamond, and
      - a `repeated_singular` annotation.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /2
    select_line: true
    search: repeated_singular

  - text: |
      The shadowed instance is also flagged:
      - a `shadowed_scalar` annotation,
      - a hollow amber diamond - press `^` to see it at the left edge of the line.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /1
    select_line: true
    search: shadowed_scalar

  - text: |
      You can navigate the protobuf using the arrow keys.
      And click on the triangles to fold/unfold nodes.

      👋 Fold the `location_bias` node to step.

    node: /7
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - not:
        - visible: /7/1

  - text: |
      Let's move on.

      👋 Press Enter to quit.

    node: /1
    command: quit
